WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.550
A closed umbrella, one
point two metres long.

2
00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:04.960
A flat box.

3
00:00:05.010 --> 00:00:09.200
Inside, it measures one metre
by nought point eight metres.

4
00:00:09.250 --> 00:00:12.770
Lay the umbrella along the
long side, and it sticks out.

5
00:00:12.820 --> 00:00:15.290
Along the short side, it's even worse.

6
00:00:15.340 --> 00:00:18.480
So is there any way to lay it flat inside?

7
00:00:18.530 --> 00:00:21.040
Or is the box just too small?

8
00:00:21.090 --> 00:00:26.020
In this mission, you'll see how a diagonal
cuts a rectangle into a pair of right-angled

9
00:00:26.070 --> 00:00:27.150
triangles.

10
00:00:27.200 --> 00:00:30.820
You'll find the hypotenuse, the
side opposite the right angle.

11
00:00:30.870 --> 00:00:33.000
It's always the longest side.

12
00:00:33.050 --> 00:00:35.500
And you'll use Pythagoras' theorem.

13
00:00:35.550 --> 00:00:40.100
The squares on the two shorter sides
add up to the square on the hypotenuse.

14
00:00:40.150 --> 00:00:44.120
Your mission: decide whether the
umbrella fits flat in the box.
